 ### Encode-Decode-Scene
-A hybrid training method that uses a weighted combination of the Encode-Scene loss ($L_E$) and Decode-Scene loss ($L_D$) to train the latent NeRF, ensuring both latent consistency and high-fidelity RGB reconstruction [S2, unofficial]. It utilizes both the encoder and decoder modules of a 3D-aware autoencoder [S2, unofficial]. The steps are: 1. Encode input images to latent space. 2. Train Tri-Planes in latent space. 3. Decode rendered latent images. 4. Compute loss in RGB space or latent space, or a combination [S2, unofficial]. The optimization objective is:
+A hybrid training method that uses a weighted combination of the Encode-Scene loss ($L_E$) and Decode-Scene loss ($L_D$) to train the latent NeRF, ensuring both latent consistency and high-fidelity RGB reconstruction [S2, unofficial]. It utilizes both the encoder and decoder modules of a 3D-aware autoencoder [S2, unofficial]. The steps are: 1. Encode input images to latent space [S2, unofficial]. 2. Train Tri-Planes in latent space [S2, unofficial]. 3. Decode rendered latent images [S2, unofficial]. 4. Compute loss in RGB space or latent space, or a combination [S2, unofficial]. The optimization objective is:
 $$ \min_{\alpha, T} (1-t)L_D(\alpha, T) + tL_E(\alpha, T) $$
 where $t \in (0, 1)$ is a mixing coefficient [S2, unofficial]. This method combines the accelerated training of Encode-Scene with the high-fidelity color output supervision of Decode-Scene [S2, unofficial].
 
 ### Encoder Training via Synthetic Data
-A method for training an encoder to predict latent codes and canonical maps using data generated from an unconditional generator, avoiding the need for ground-truth 3D meshes or hand-modeled synthetic meshes required by NOCS [S3]. The steps are: 1. Sample a minibatch of priors $z \sim N(0, I)$. 2. Feed priors through a mapping network to obtain latent codes $w \in W$. 3. Train the network (e.g., SegFormer with a custom regression head) to predict the canonical map and latent code $w$ from the RGB image [S3]. A key pitfall in related methods like NOCS is the requirement for ground-truth 3D meshes or hand-modeled synthetic meshes representative of the training dataset, which are not available on real datasets [S3].
